    <annotation id="prefigure-lagrange-lifeguard-figure" speech2="A horizontal shoreline separates the sand, below, from the water, above. The lifeguard is at the point A on the sand, a distance a from the shoreline, and the swimmer at the point B in the water, a distance b from it. The route, drawn in orange, runs straight from A to a point P on the shoreline and then straight from P to B. Along the shoreline, P is a distance x from the point opposite A and a distance y from the point opposite B. A dashed line through P is perpendicular to the shoreline. The run makes a large angle, theta 1, with it, and the swim a small angle, theta 2.">
